          "number": 11,
          "letter": "K",
          "english": "Facts don't change our minds. Friendship does. Years ago, Ben Casnocha mentioned an idea to me that I haven't been able to shake: The people who are most likely to change our minds are the ones we agree with on 98 percent of topics. If someone you know, like, and trust believes a radical idea, you are more likely to give it merit, weight, or consideration. You already agree with them in most areas of life. Maybe you should change your mind on this one too. But if someone wildly different than you proposes the same radical idea, well, it's easy to dismiss them as nuts.",
          "chinese": "事实不能改变我们的想法，友谊可以。多年前，本·卡斯诺查向我提到一个想法，我一直无法摆脱它：最有可能改变我们想法的人，是那些在98%的话题上与我们意见一致的人。如果一个你认识、喜欢并信任的人相信一个激进的观点，你就更有可能认为这个观点有道理、有分量，或值得考虑。你已经在生活的大多数方面与他意见一致。也许这一次你也应该改变自己的想法。但如果一个与你截然不同的人提出同样的激进观点，那么，把他当成疯子而不予理会就很容易了。",
